    {
      "type": "caption",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "Figure 5-7. Word and Byte Write-Cycle Timing Diagram",
      "bbox": [
        566,
        1273,
        1611,
        1317
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_003"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "The descriptions of the eight states of a write cycle are as follows:",
      "bbox": [
        289,
        1374,
        1457,
        1416
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_004"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 0 The write cycle starts in S0. The processor places valid function codes on FC2–FC0 and drives $R/\\overline{W}$ high (if a preceding write cycle has left $R/\\overline{W}$ low).",
      "bbox": [
        290,
        1438,
        1896,
        1525
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_005"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 1 Entering S1, the processor drives a valid address on the address bus.",
      "bbox": [
        290,
        1571,
        1768,
        1613
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_006"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 2 On the rising edge of S2, the processor asserts $\\overline{AS}$ and drives $R/\\overline{W}$ low.",
      "bbox": [
        290,
        1654,
        1800,
        1700
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_007"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 3 During S3, the data bus is driven out of the high-impedance state as the data to be written is placed on the bus.",
      "bbox": [
        290,
        1745,
        1902,
        1831
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_008"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 4 At the rising edge of S4, the processor asserts $\\overline{UDS}$, or $\\overline{LDS}$. The processor waits for a cycle termination signal ($\\overline{DTACK}$ or $\\overline{BERR}$) or $\\overline{VPA}$, an M6800 peripheral signal. When $\\overline{VPA}$ is asserted during S4, the cycle becomes a peripheral cycle (refer to **Appendix B M6800 Peripheral Interface**. If neither termination signal is asserted before the falling edge at the end of S4, the processor inserts wait states (full clock cycles) until either $\\overline{DTACK}$ or $\\overline{BERR}$ is asserted.",
      "bbox": [
        290,
        1874,
        1908,
        2193
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_009"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 5 During S5, no bus signals are altered.",
      "bbox": [
        292,
        2243,
        1211,
        2286
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_010"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "STATE 6 During S6, no bus signals are altered.",
      "bbox": [
        292,
        2330,
        1211,
        2372
      ],
      "segment_id": "page_0031_seg_011"
    },
    {
      "type": "footer",
      "continuation": false,
      "heading_level": null,
      "md_text": "5-6",
